# GoPasig Core Standards

## Stack

Laravel (PHP), Blade, Tailwind CSS v4, Vite. Fleet/transit domain: admin, dispatcher (fleet), driver, commuter roles.

## Clean architecture

```
HTTP Request → Route → Middleware → Controller → Form Request / Service → Model → View or JSON
```

- **Routes**: map URLs only; avoid closures with business logic.
- **Controllers**: thin — coordinate and return responses.
- **Form Requests**: validation and request-level auth (see `LoginRequest`).
- **Services** (`app/Services/`): business rules when controllers grow.
- **Models**: data access, relationships, scopes.
- **Views**: presentation only; use Blade components.

## Anti-spaghetti rules

- Do not duplicate markup — use Blade components in `resources/views/components/`.
- Do not put queries or role logic in Blade or route closures.
- Prefer one class per responsibility over god files.
- Minimize scope of each change; match existing naming and folder layout.

## Security defaults

- `@csrf` on state-changing web forms.
- Validate all input via Form Requests.
- Role protection via middleware (`role:admin`, etc.) or policies.

## Subagents

Delegate when appropriate: `/frontend`, `/backend`, `/debugging`, `/database`.
